<section class="chat-section" aria-labelledby="chat-heading"><div class="chat-intro"><h2 id="chat-heading">Everyone gets a face</h2><p>One name per person, and the string does the rest. The same handle always produces the same blobatar, so whoever you learn in a thread is who you recognise in the sidebar.</p></div>
<div class="chat-card"><header class="chat-header"><span><span class="muted">#</span> release</span><div class="facepile"><% %w[laura tobias svea ivan].each do |name| %><%= blobatar_tag name, title: name, size: 28 %><% end %><span class="facepile-extra">+12</span></div></header><div class="chat-messages">
<% [ ['laura', '9:41', ['shipped the new avatars — every account has one now', 'no uploads, no grey initials']], ['tobias', '9:42', ["wait, they’re generated from the username?"]], ['svea', '9:43', ['same string, same face, forever. mine has looked like this since I signed up']], ['ivan', '9:43', ['so staging me and prod me are different people 😅']], ['svea', '9:44', ["different string, different person. that’s the whole trick"]] ].each do |name, time, messages| %>
  <div class="chat-message"><%= blobatar_tag name, animate: :hover, size: 40, title: "Blobatar for #{name}" %><div><div class="message-heading"><strong><%= name %></strong><time><%= time %></time></div><% messages.each do |message| %><p><%= message %></p><% end %></div></div>
<% end %><div class="chat-typing"><%= blobatar_tag 'tobias', animate: :hover, size: 40, title: 'tobias is typing' %><span class="typing-dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>tobias is typing</span></div></div></div></section>
